<title>INDIA: BSE figures of India carry forward trade - Sept 28.</title>
<headline>BSE figures of India carry forward trade - Sept 28.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is the latest data, for the top 10 stocks by value, released by the Bombay Stock Exchange (BSE) for the carry forward or &quot;badla&quot; account ended September 28</p>
<p>SCRIP		  SETTLEMENT  AV BADLA  QTY    VALUE    % BADLA</p>
<p>			 RATE				 (RS MLN)</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>State Bank	   250	   0.72     380700  95.18    15.02</p>
<p>Tata Steel	   168	   0.46     433950  72.90    14.28</p>
<p>Reliance	     186	   0.51     266800  49.62    14.30</p>
<p>L&amp;T		    233	   0.64     135200  31.50    14.32</p>
<p>ACC		   1763	   5.07	15890  28.01    15.00</p>
<p>Tata Power	   127	   0.36     200300  25.44    14.78</p>
<p>Tata Engg	    450	   1.09	40500  18.23    12.63</p>
<p>BSES Ltd	     174	   0.50	83500  14.53    14.98</p>
<p>IPCL		   112	   0.27     111700  12.51    12.57</p>
<p>Colgate		247	   0.57	34700   8.57    12.03</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>The average badla charges work out to 13.70 percent on an annualised basis against 16.18 percent in the previous carry forward account ended Sept 21. -- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
